rec:
Her family | Pragmatic and quietly independent. Her father works in resource extraction. Her mother runs the household and treats Imperial loyalty as a practical arrangement rather than a conviction (TR).
Her Dominion | Texas negotiated its surrender and kept the attitude. Lone performs loyalty loudly and then does what it was going to do anyway, and its outer-territory women have an autonomy that would get them flagged in Aurem (DOM).
In the Trials | If a Lone girl is selected she goes, the Dominion supports her adequately, and nobody gets emotional about the outcome. Lone directness: do the thing, see what happens (DOM).
prompt: What she was thinking about for two years before she filed | fill

@page rh="THE COVENANT DAUGHTERS · IX · VIVIENNE · FAITH AND SCRIPTURE · 1 OF 2" m="TKC: TR · DOM; VOL. I · {v1:lone} · {v1:lived4}"
# What she believes
rec:
Who taught her | A mother for whom loyalty is a practical arrangement (TR). The First Ride, a long distance navigated alone while the community waits. The Giving, something of a grandmother's handed to a bride (DOM).
What she believes | OPEN QUESTION: Curiosity is the only creed on file (TR).
What she practices | Burial with boots on, ready for wherever the dead go next (DOM).
empire: What the Temple teaches about a woman like her
POSSIBLE: Lone gets Proverbs 31.27, "She looketh well to the ways of her household," and the Governor-Prelate never checks whether anyone listened (DOM).
/end
