@page rh="THE COVENANT DAUGHTERS · IX · VIVIENNE · FAITH AND SCRIPTURE · 2 OF 2" m="1 KGS 10.1–7; MATT 12.42; NUM 13.25–33; JOSH 2"
# The text
rec:
Her name | *Vivienne* has no biblical source. It's from the Latin *vivus*, "alive."
The queen of Sheba · 1 Kings 10 | POSSIBLE: She comes from far away to see for herself, asks hard questions, and says "the half was not told me" (10.7). **Where it breaks:** Sheba goes home with gifts and a story she's free to tell. Vivienne goes home with information nobody in Covenant Basin can use (TR).
The spies · Numbers 13 | POSSIBLE: Twelve men sent to look at a land and come back with a report. **Where it breaks:** Their report is public, and argued over. Vivienne's report is hers.
tab:
| She'd quote | Never read to her |
| 1 Kings 10.7, "the half was not told me" | Joshua 2, a woman who reads the whole war correctly from her window |
box: Volume One
Lone, {v1:lone}. Lived religion, {v1:lived4}. Rahab, {v1:ruth}. Numbers, the count and the camp, {v1:f1-count}.
/end

